// aug14f overnight swarm (2026-08-15): 11 of the round's 17 live
// witnesses were this one seam. `Kernel::update`'s bottom-result arm
// returned the shared bottom WITHOUT persisting it ("the resident
// keeps the last genuine result", written at the 5c flip) — so the
// next quiet cycle's R1 ride re-served Stale(pre-bottom value), a
// REAL value, where the interp op's resident (node/op.rs) goes
// StaleBottom. A de-fused consumer (here: the interpreted select's
// arm re-match on the scrutinee's connect-cycle fire) read the ridden
// value, re-fired it as Fired, and the downstream product kernel
// emitted it — jit [1:0] on an epoch the interp holds bottom-quiet.
// Boundary matrix (each one ingredient off the diverging case):
//   const-bottom untaken arm (de-fuses the select) ....... DIVERGE
//   untaken arm i64:5 (whole select fuses, seam gone) .... agree
//   final epoch in0=2 (no fresh bottom in taken arm) ..... agree
//   without the `v1: i64` annotation ..................... DIVERGE
// Fix: persist the bottom into the resident (the interp op twin) —
// the kernel face of the standing-bottoms genus, sibling of
// formal-bottom-persists-aug2026.
// schedule-v1: cap=112 events=896; in0=i64:1; in0=i64:0
{let v0 = i64:0; v0 <- in0; let v1: i64 = select v0 {i64:-1 => cast<i64>(null)$, _ => i64:-100 % (in0 + i64:0)}; v0 * v1}
